  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "brief",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "StyleNow \u2014 design pass\n\nMatched to the shipped tokens in apps/web/src/app/globals.css: Poppins/Inter, coral #f0566e on cream #fff9f3, teal/amber/violet accents, radii 12/16/22/28, pill controls. Nothing rounded to a grid.\n\nWhat changed and why is on the 'Design vocabulary' board, page 2."
    },
    {
      "id": "photo-note",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2570,
      "w": 390,
      "text": "The cover is a marked placeholder. A salon page really wants photography here \u2014 it is the biggest remaining gap, and no drawing substitutes for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "sidebar-note",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "The one deliberate departure from the shipped app: the seven-tab bar becomes a left spine. A tab bar is a customer-app pattern; a tool open eight hours a day wants persistent navigation with room for live counts."
    },
    {
      "id": "staff-note",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Employee calendar, and the loop it opens up.\n\nThe shop calendar answers \"what is the salon doing\". These answer \"what am I doing\" \u2014 a different question, and the one a stylist actually asks. The week board frames it as sold hours against rostered hours, which turns \"Thursday is quiet\" into \"Thursday is eight paid hours nobody bought\".\n\nThat number is what the waiting-list board then acts on. The app already tells a shop \"2 on the waiting list can be called\" and gives it nowhere to call them."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "page-3"
  }
